I. Definitions

"Software" means the LayerCut source code, binaries and documentation.
"Author" means the copyright holder NukumizuKazuhiko.
"Output Files" means any file directly or indirectly generated, exported
or rendered by the Software or a modified version, including but not
limited to exported images (PNG etc.), vector graphics (SVG etc.) and
project files. Following the drafting style of Apache-2.0's "Derivative
Works" definition, this definition deliberately brings such outputs
within the scope of this license, whereas Apache-2.0 excludes them.
"Commercial Use" means any of the following:
  (a) providing a network service with the Software or a modified version
      (including SaaS, online tools, APIs);
  (b) making the Software or a modified version into a commercial product
      that is sold or offered for a fee;
  (c) distributing the Software or a modified version bundled with, given
      away with, or packaged as part of other commercial goods or services;
  (d) using Output Files produced by the Software or a modified version
      for commercial purposes, including but not limited to selling the
      Output Files, incorporating them into commercial goods or services,
      or using them in for-profit production activities (such as physical
      fabrication, printing or cutting work sold afterwards).
"Notice" means an email to the Author at: mihoyostart@gmail.com.
"Contributor" means the Author and any person or organization that
submits code, documentation, icons or other modifications to the
Software; a "Contribution" means such submitted content.

II. Grant

Subject to the sole condition in Section III, any person or organization
may use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense and sell the
Software and modified versions, free of charge, perpetually and
irrevocably — including every Commercial Use scenario above.

III. Sole Condition: Commercial Notice

3.1 Upon starting any Commercial Use, the user shall send a Notice to the
    Author, containing only: the name of the user (person/organization),
    the form of use (a/b/c/d above), and the start date. For item (d),
    "upon starting" means when the Output Files are first used for
    commercial purposes; the same user needs to send a Notice only once
    per form of use.
3.2 The Notice is a synchronous obligation: it takes effect upon sending.
    No confirmation, reply or permission from the Author is required; the
    Author's lack of reply or disagreement does not affect the legality
    of the use.
3.3 Non-commercial personal study, research, internal evaluation and
    local use do not require a Notice.

IV. Patent License

4.1 Subject to the terms of this license, each Contributor grants every
    recipient of the Software a perpetual, worldwide, non-exclusive,
    no-charge, royalty-free, irrevocable (except as stated in 4.2)
    patent license to make, have made, use, offer to sell, sell,
    import, and otherwise transfer the Software, modified versions and
    Output Files. "Licensable patent claims" means patent claims owned
    or controlled by that Contributor, licensable by them, that are
    necessarily infringed by their Contribution alone, or by
    combination of their Contribution with the Software.
4.2 Termination for patent litigation: if any person institutes patent
    litigation against any entity (including a cross-claim or
    counterclaim in a lawsuit) alleging that the Software, a modified
    version, Output Files or any Contribution infringes a patent, the
    patent licenses granted to that person under this Section terminate
    as of the date the litigation is filed. Termination of the patent
    license does not affect the copyright or other rights such person
    holds under the other Sections of this license.
4.3 For clarity: the patent license in this Section does not extend to
    works that are separate from the Software and modified versions, or
    that merely interface (or bind by name) to the Software.

